      "writtenOn": "2022-03-31T14:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that\u0027s true in general (and if it were, I\u0027d think we should enforce it in `Intent::createChooser()` -- where actually the Javadocs already refer to conditions for other actions). You can see for example `ChooserActivity::isSendAction()` is used internally to gate on other action types.\n\nI did notice the comments in `ChooserActivity::onCopyButtonClicked()` suggesting that we didn\u0027t need to handle other cases *there* because the copy button is (somehow?) not shown in the UI for other actions. Maybe we can make that same assertion about the edit button?\n\nStill, I would prefer to see this look something like:\n```\n} else {\n    Log.e(TAG, originalAction + \" editing is not supported\");\n    return null;\n}\n```\n(instead of or in addition to the log message that specifically describes \"multiple image edit\")\n\nSpeaking of which, do we have logic elsewhere to justify the interpretation that ACTION_SEND only shows an edit button for \"image edit\"? (E.g., do we check the content type before adding the edit button?)",
      "parentUuid": "a765412d_9521610b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1188,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1191,
        "endChar": 9
